 ### Advanced settings
 Some TV models are comptabile with a specific backend, but require a slightly different routine to work reliably. You can find an explaination for  these so called quirks [here](https://github.com/webosbrew/hyperion-webos/tree/main#quirks).
 
+### Experimental text recognition
+The modified service has an opt-in **Recognize English text** setting. It submits at most one grayscale video frame per second to the Tesseract installation on the TV and writes recognized words with bounding boxes and confidence to the hyperion-webos log. It processes the video frame before the TV UI is blended in, so the menu is not part of OCR. The feature requires `/usr/bin/tesseract` and `/usr/share/tessdata/eng.traineddata`; it is disabled by default. When enabled, both capture backends request at least 1280×720. The captured video frame is used directly for OCR and for the existing HyperHDR composition/output path; no second capture or OCR-only downscaled copy is created.
+
+For the G5 dual output profile, explicitly select 1280×720, RGB output (`nv12:false`),
+disable UI capture (`nogui:true`), enable OCR and autostart, and retain the HyperHDR
+destination `127.0.0.1:19400`. OCR runs in a separate worker with one replaceable
+pending grayscale frame; it skips a sample when the queue mutex is busy.
+Tesseract runs with `OMP_THREAD_LIMIT=1` and niceness 10. The one-frame-per-second
+setting limits submissions; completed OCR can be substantially slower.
+
+Diagnostics retain one paired capture sample per session in
+`/tmp/piccap-hyperhdr-sample.ppm`, `/tmp/piccap-ocr-sample.pgm`, and
+`/tmp/piccap-ocr-sample.tsv`. Input dimensions/stride are recorded in
+`/tmp/piccap-ocr-input.txt`. The latest TSV and actual completion count, processing
+time, and OCR throughput are available in `/tmp/piccap-ocr-latest.tsv` and
+`/tmp/piccap-ocr-status.txt`. These are bounded snapshots, not a video recording.
+For an additional current OCR input, create `/tmp/piccap-ocr-snapshot-request`.
+The worker consumes that request after a successful OCR and overwrites just
+`/tmp/piccap-ocr-snapshot.pgm` and its matching `.tsv`. It does not start another
+capture or change the existing output profile.
+
+The sender completes partial TCP writes before starting another FlatBuffers
+packet, reads complete reply headers/payloads, validates replies, and reconnects
+after a failed partial send. Invalid capture frames are not sent to HyperHDR.
+
 ## Development
 ### Dependencies
 To build PicCap and hyperion-webos you will need:  
@@ -89,6 +114,11 @@ npm run-script build-backend    # Build hyperion-webos + deps only
 npm run-script package
 ```  
 
+Packaging also requires Python 3 (standard library only). The package wrapper
+preserves mode 0755 for the native executable and service scripts even when
+`ares-package` runs on Windows. The boot hook uses the supported `status` method
+to activate the native service; the persisted autostart option starts capture.
+
